"""Build the offline radical-state appendix from the verified data."""
from pathlib import Path
from html import escape
import json

root=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
data=json.loads((root/'verified.json').read_text())
def tex(t):return '<div class="formula" data-tex="'+escape(t,quote=True)+'"></div>'
formulae=[
    r't=\frac{\sqrt{2447347+310013\sqrt{61}}-991-159\sqrt{61}}{2050}',
    r'z=5(15-\sqrt{61})t,\qquad u=\frac{t(4tz-29t-z+8)}{-84tz+336t+z^2-25}',
    r'Q=1+84u+84t^2+uz^2',
    r'|\psi_9\rangle=\frac1{\sqrt Q}\left(|D_9^{(0)}\rangle+\sqrt{84u}|D_9^{(3)}\rangle+\sqrt{84}\,t|D_9^{(6)}\rangle+z\sqrt u|D_9^{(9)}\rangle\right)',
    r'S_5(|\psi_9\rangle)=\frac{130928+6832\sqrt{61}}{1461}\simeq126.1380053290857377280590'
]
rows=''.join(f'<tr><td>{r}</td><td>{float(c):.15f}</td></tr>' for r,c in zip(data['support'],data['coefficients']))
precision='\n'.join(f'c_{r} = {c}' for r,c in zip(data['support'],data['coefficients']))
html='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Nine-qubit S₅ radical state · Extremal symmetric states</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="../../styles.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="../../vendor/katex/katex.min.css"><script src="../../vendor/katex/katex.min.js" defer></script><style>.formula{overflow-x:auto;margin:1.4rem 0;padding:.5rem 0}.precision{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;background:#f0f1eb;font-size:.8rem;line-height:1.7;padding:1.2rem}summary{cursor:pointer}.coefficient-table{max-width:570px;margin:1.5rem 0}.scope-note{border-left:3px solid #326557;padding-left:1.2rem}</style></head><body class="research-page"><header class="site-header"><a class="wordmark" href="../../index.html#n=9&k=5&mode=max">← Sector-length catalogue</a><nav><a href="#state">Exact state</a><a href="#verify">Verification</a><a href="../algebraic-s6/index.html">S₆ minima</a></nav></header><main><section class="intro"><div class="intro-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Exact radical reconstruction · 28 October 2026</p><h1>A radical form<br><em>for the S₅ maximizer</em></h1><p class="intro-description">The proved nine-qubit maximum admits explicit nested radicals for every Dicke coefficient and a quadratic expression for its sector value.</p></div><div class="intro-aside"><span class="section-number">N = 9</span><p>Sector k = 5<br>Proved global maximum</p><a href="verified.json" download>100-digit coefficients ↓</a></div></section><section class="reference-section research-method" id="state"><h2>The exact representative</h2><p class="scope-note">The formulas below establish an exact stationary state and its attained value. Global maximality is now established by a separate <a href="../n9-s5-maximum/index.html">exact algebraic SOS certificate</a>.</p><p>Define the real parameters t, z and u as follows. The selected branch has t &lt; 0, z &lt; 0 and u &gt; 0; every square root denotes its positive real value.</p>'''+''.join(tex(t) for t in formulae)+'''<p>All coefficients outside Dicke indices 0, 3, 6 and 9 vanish.</p><table class="gap-table coefficient-table"><thead><tr><th>Dicke index r</th><th>Coefficient</th></tr></thead><tbody>'''+rows+'''</tbody></table><details><summary>100-digit coefficients</summary><pre class="precision">'''+escape(precision)+'''</pre></details><p><a href="parametrization.json" download>Exact formulas (JSON) ↓</a> · <a href="../../index.html#n=9&k=5&mode=max">Open catalogue record ↗</a></p></section><section class="reference-section research-method" id="verify"><h2>How the radical form was obtained</h2><p>Use binomial-scaled amplitudes on support 0, 3, 6 and 9. Exact elimination of the normalized stationary equations yields the parameter polynomial</p>'''+tex(r'20500t^4+39640t^3-10178t^2+252t+5=0.')+'''<p>It factors over the field generated by the square root of 61. The selected branch obeys</p>'''+tex(r't^2+\frac{991+159\sqrt{61}}{1025}t+\frac{15+\sqrt{61}}{820}=0.')+'''<p>The quadratic formula gives the displayed t; rational reconstruction supplies z and u. Exact reductions verify all stationary equations and the sector value. Rational interval arithmetic verifies the root choice, nonzero denominators and positive square-root branches. Full complex stationarity follows from the exact equations, the threefold rotation symmetry and complex-conjugation invariance.</p><p>An independent high-precision calculation reproduces the state. Numerical Hessian checks give 15 negative physical directions after removing normalization, global phase and collective rotations. This supports local maximality and does not establish global optimality.</p><p>Run from the website directory with Python 3, SymPy and mpmath:</p><pre class="precision">python3 research/algebraic-s5-n9/verify.py</pre><p><a href="verify.py">Read the verifier</a> · <a href="../n9-s5-maximum/index.html">Global optimality proof and exact certificate ↗</a> · <a href="../algebraic-s6/index.html">Algebraic coefficients for the N = 10, 11, 12 S₆ minima ↗</a></p></section></main><footer class="site-footer"><p>Extremal symmetric states</p><a href="../../index.html">Return to catalogue ↑</a></footer><script>document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded',()=>{document.querySelectorAll('[data-tex]').forEach(el=>el.innerHTML=katex.renderToString(el.dataset.tex,{displayMode:true,throwOnError:false,trust:false}))});</script></body></html>'''
